  "verdict_rule": "The 95 percent paired bootstrap interval for log10(a0_B/a0_A) decides the label: entirely above zero gives TENSION_JOINT_CHANNEL_B_ABOVE_CHANNEL_A, entirely below zero gives TENSION_JOINT_CHANNEL_B_BELOW_CHANNEL_A, otherwise CONSISTENT_INTERVAL_CONTAINS_ZERO. The rule is symmetric in direction. An interval containing zero is compatible with every model that reproduces both relations, including the standard null, and is not evidence for OPH. A tension counts only against this declared submodel with its declared conventions, never against the framework beyond that scope."
